# apps/web environment — foundation build (Phase 01), extended in Phase 03 (FIX-1)
#
# The browser-visible surface is ONE variable: the WebSocket URL of our own
# voice service. Live providers and storage are configured server-side, so
# the values below are read by the Next.js server only.
#
# Rules for later phases:
# - Never place provider API keys or service-role keys in NEXT_PUBLIC_*
#   variables: public-prefixed values are inlined into the browser bundle
#   and are readable by anyone who opens the page.
# - The browser must talk to our own voice service, not directly to a
#   speech provider, so provider keys stay server-side.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VOICE_WS_URL — the WebSocket URL of the voice service the
# browser opens the call socket on. It is inlined at build time.
# Defaults to ws://localhost:8000/ws/call when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VOICE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000/ws/call
#
# Supabase (Phase 06) — server-side values. They are deliberately NOT
# NEXT_PUBLIC_: the publishable key is not a server secret, but only the
# Next.js server reads these, and nothing about them belongs in the bundle.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
